# Lyric
Coltrane knew the shape of time
every note a tunnel through the noise
the instanton finds the lowest path
between where you are and where you must go

The saxophone does not choose its notes
the notes choose themselves
through the reed through the breath
through the curve of the brass

Change is a tunnel through probability
the music finds the path of least resistance
and that path sounds like beauty
and that path sounds like truth

Giant Steps are not steps at all
they are the space between steps
the instanton lives in that space
the instanton is the space

Coltrane knew what physics knows
the shortest path through noise is melody
the shortest path through silence is song<|endoftext|>
